1
00:00:20,840 --> 00:00:31,435
I have slept in this corner for years in the grass, 
under moss and the shade of the old taxus tree,

2
00:00:31,527 --> 00:00:43,752
And I watch as the rusty gate creaks in the wind, 
and you bring a sweet boy here to meet little me.

3
00:00:47,478 --> 00:00:58,046
The sun hides away as you step on my ground, 
and the air turns so chilly and suddenly grey,

4
00:00:58,221 --> 00:01:11,090
But my heart is so glad as you stand by my grave, 
and you wipe all the damp of the morning away.

5
00:01:30,187 --> 00:01:40,678
I have watched you grow up from my place in the quiet, 
through the years of long silence that filled our old home,

6
00:01:40,791 --> 00:01:53,008
Where the tears fell like rain in the shadows of mother, 
and you felt so afraid and so deeply alone.

7
00:01:56,781 --> 00:02:07,427
But I see how he holds you, 
I feel how his warmth is now breaking the ice that had frozen your heart,

8
00:02:07,515 --> 00:02:20,152
And I wanted to whisper that you should be happy, 
and ready for all of your new lives to start.

9
00:02:39,498 --> 00:02:50,625
But now look at the boy bending down to the dirt, 
to the gravel and stones where the wild weeds grow,

10
00:02:50,768 --> 00:03:03,148
To find a small pebble, so perfectly round, 
like a tear made of clay that is starting to glow.

11
00:03:05,997 --> 00:03:16,849
And he places it tenderly on my cold name, 
as a silent promise that you’re not alone,

12
00:03:16,894 --> 00:03:31,051
That my memory lives and your love will remain, 
as pure as the light on this smooth white stone.

13
00:03:33,149 --> 00:03:43,658
I sing through the dove in the high branches now, 
and I watch as the sun paints the graveyard in gold,

14
00:03:43,800 --> 00:03:57,125
The chill of my winter is fading away, 
as I watch the two of you gently unfold.

15
00:03:59,880 --> 00:04:09,977
You smile through your tears as he kisses your cheek, 
and I promise you both that my spirit is free,

16
00:04:10,118 --> 00:04:23,194
So hold each other tight in the warmth of the day, 
and live out your lives for yourselves and for me.

